WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.634
-Republicans and right-wing
pundits are focusing

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:07.000
on the leak of
the Supreme Court's draft ruling

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.000
overturning Roe v. Wade,
rather than the ruling itself.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.534
Meanwhile, more evidence
is emerging that potentially

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:14.534
links Donald Trump
to the militia groups

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:16.868
involved in the attempted coup
on January 6th.

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:19.534
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:26.667
The right has been trying
to overturn Roe for 50 years,

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:28.200
and in order
to achieve that goal,

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.501
they've broken every
conceivable norm in their path

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:32.167
and nearly detonated
our democracy.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:34.467
In fact, they partnered
with a monstrous demagogue

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.167
who literally tried
to overthrow our democracy.

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:39.133
And as part of
that Faustian bargain,

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:42.000
Trump promised to give them
the judges they wanted

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.501
as long as
they looked the other way

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:46.334
during his many crimes
and abuses, and for years,

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:48.634
Trump has gone out of his way
to remind Republicans

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:51.634
of the judges he gave them in
order to retain their loyalty.

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:54.634
-I've always heard
how important judges are.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.901
Now we know
how important they are.

00:00:56.901 --> 00:01:01.267
I have 252 beautiful,
brand-new, conservative,

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:02.601
wonderful judges.

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:06.767
We have confirmed 191

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:09.567
brand-new, beautiful
federal judges.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:12.400
All those judges,
those beautiful judges.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.467
-No matter what
he's talking about,

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:16.167
he makes it sound
like real estate.

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:18.734
[As Trump] We have so many
brand-new, beautiful,

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:21.434
split-level judges,
all new appliances,

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:23.067
ready now for an easy move.

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:26.067
These judges won't last.
Book a viewing today.

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:27.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.868
[Normal voice] Trump got
the GOP over the finish line,

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.801
but this plot
did not begin with him,

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:33.567
and it's not unique
to his presidency.

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:36.534
Overturning Roe has been
a nearly singular,

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:39.400
obsessive goal of the extremist
right for half a century,

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.701
as Senator Elizabeth Warren
noted after a protest

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.701
outside the Supreme Court
on Tuesday.

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:48.033
-The Republicans have been
working toward this day

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:49.701
for decades.

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:51.868
They have been
out there plotting,

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:55.734
carefully cultivating these
Supreme Court justices

00:01:55.734 --> 00:01:59.100
so they could have a majority
on the bench

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.334
who would accomplish something

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:04.200
that the majority of Americans
do not want.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.601
-It's true,
they've spent decades

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.267
carefully cultivating
these justices.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:09.534
They look like they were
grown in a lab

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:10.701
to overturn abortion rights.

00:02:10.701 --> 00:02:12.033
I mean, look at this guy.

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:14.734
He looks like the dean
who threatens

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:17.868
to shut down the fraternity
in every '80s teen comedy.

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:20.334
If he had written
the draft opinion,

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:21.501
it would have ended with,

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.601
"We rule that Roe
must be overturned

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:27.167
and also that a werewolf
can't play basketball!"

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:28.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:30.067
Of course, it won't surprise you
to learn that

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:32.534
instead of responding
to the substance

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:35.234
that Warren and the protesters
are saying, the depraved weirdos

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:36.534
who make up today's
Republican Party

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:39.100
decided instead to mock
the people who attended.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.634
For example, there's Florida
Congressman Matt Gaetz,

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:43.400
who is currently under
federal investigation

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.133
over unpaid parking tickets --
Wait. Sorry, I read that wrong.

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:47.801
Over whether he had
a sexual relationship

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:49.934
with a 17-year-old and paid
for her to travel with him

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:52.334
in violation of federal
sex trafficking laws.

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:55.634
And I'm sure he also hasn't paid
all his parking tickets.

00:02:55.634 --> 00:02:58.734
Gaetz chose a line of attack
that quickly backfired.

00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:01.901
-One lawmaker appearing to stoke
the flames of controversy,

00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:04.234
Florida Congressman
Matt Gaetz tweeting,

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:07.133
"How many of the women
rallying against overturning Roe

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:10.000
are over-educated,
under-loved millennials

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.601
who sadly return from protests
to a lonely microwave dinner

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:16.868
with their cats,
and no Bumble matches?"

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:21.400
-It is very telling that you
think "overeducated" is a burn.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.901
"So, what grade are you in?"

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:24.234
"Oh, I'm a sophomore
in college."

00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:28.334
"Sophomore? Sorry, you're
a little overeducated for me.

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:30.334
Once you've read
'Fahrenheit 451,'

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:32.801
you're basically a grandma
to ol' Gaetzy!"

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:34.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.133
When they're not
mocking protesters,

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:37.400
they are, of course,

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.067
pretending to be indignant
over the leak itself,

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:41.634
rather than celebrating
the outcome,

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:43.534
because they know
overturning Roe

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:46.467
and criminalizing abortion
are deeply unpopular

00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:48.200
with a huge majority
of voters.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:51.067
So, instead, they want
to throw the leaker in jail.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:54.234
-What happened to the court
today was the saddest chapter

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:56.267
in the history of
the United States Supreme Court.

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:59.234
This was despicable,
it's dangerous, and it was dumb.

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:01.968
-If that left-wing
law clerk succeeds,

00:04:01.968 --> 00:04:04.968
it will be the most
grotesque politicization

00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:08.000
of the Supreme Court
in the history of our nation.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.767
You mentioned
an FBI investigation.

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.734
I hope there is a serious one.

00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:13.868
And I hope whoever
is responsible for this

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.901
not only is fired instantly,

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:19.400
but is prosecuted
and serves real jail time

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.400
for violating the confidences
of the Supreme Court.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.100
-There is no duo in history

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.767
worse than Ted Cruz
and Lindsey Graham.

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:27.701
You know who was
a much better duo?

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:29.634
Milli Vanilli.

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:31.868
Or as they're known
in Supreme Court parlance,

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:33.467
Milli v. Anilli.

00:04:33.467 --> 00:04:34.901
Next time...

00:04:34.901 --> 00:04:37.968
Next time Cruz flees his state
during a weather emergency.

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:39.133
I'm betting he'll...

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:41.133
-♪ Blame it on the rain ♪

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:42.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:45.667
By the way, if you got
that musical reference,

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:47.834
Matt Gaetz doesn't want
to date you.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:50.300
[ Laughter and applause ]
Anyway...

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.634
If you want to talk
about politicizing the court,

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:55.167
why don't we talk about the fact
that a sitting justice,

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:57.667
Clarence Thomas,
was the sole vote

00:04:57.667 --> 00:05:00.234
in a case that would have
allowed Trump to keep documents

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:02.367
relevant to the January 6th
insurrection private --

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:04.200
documents, it turns out,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.000
that could have involved
Thomas' wife, Ginni Thomas,

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.801
who repeatedly
sent text messages

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:10.200
to Trump's chief of staff

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.367
pushing him to overturn
the 2020 election.

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:15.400
Thomas didn't recuse himself
from that case.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.400
His wife was texting Meadows
insane theories

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.300
about election fraud and ideas
for how to keep Trump in power.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.200
And really,
I cannot stress enough

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.868
how unhinged these texts were.

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:27.334
-The Washington Post obtained
copies of messages

00:05:27.334 --> 00:05:29.968
that had been turned over
to the January 6 committee,

00:05:29.968 --> 00:05:31.367
revealing that Ginni Thomas

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:33.767
sent former Trump
Chief of Staff Mark Meadows

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:38.067
a barrage of texts in the weeks
after the 2020 election,

00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:40.834
urging him to try
to overturn the results.

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:43.801
She referred to wild,
far-right conspiracy theories,

00:05:43.801 --> 00:05:47.033
sending Meadows a link
to an absolutely

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:49.701
just insane YouTube video
that's since been taken down,

00:05:49.701 --> 00:05:52.567
which was centered around
a fake QAnon conspiracy theory.

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:54.734
After she texted
that video to Meadows,

00:05:54.734 --> 00:05:57.234
"Thomas added, quote,
I hope this is true."

00:05:57.234 --> 00:05:59.534
-Right after the election,
she quoted to Meadows

00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:02.601
the language then circulating
on pro-Trump sites.

00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:07.300
Quote, "Biden crime family and
ballot fraud co-conspirators

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:11.000
(elected officials, bureaucrats,
social media censorship mongers,

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.267
fake stream media
reporters, etc)

00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:17.167
are being arrested and detained
for ballot fraud right now

00:06:17.167 --> 00:06:21.167
and over coming days, and will
be living in barges off Gitmo

00:06:21.167 --> 00:06:23.734
to face military tribunals
for sedition,"

00:06:23.734 --> 00:06:25.968
adding, "I hope this is true."

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:27.367
-Now, Ginni.

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:30.367
Personally, when a text ends
with "I hope this is true,"

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:32.400
I prefer that it follows
something like,

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:33.934
"Heard you're coming home
for the holidays,"

00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:36.767
or, "A little bird told me
you got that promotion."

00:06:36.767 --> 00:06:41.067
Not "Biden crime family will be
living in barges off Gitmo,"

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:43.567
you cuckoo nut-bird!

00:06:43.567 --> 00:06:45.400
Do you travel
with a life preserver?

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:48.367
Because, lady, you are
off the [bleep] deep end.

00:06:48.367 --> 00:06:51.701
And you may say, "Eh, she's not
a Supreme Court justice.

00:06:51.701 --> 00:06:53.200
She's his wife.
Leave her alone."

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.334
First of all, it's a massive
conflict of interest.

00:06:55.334 --> 00:06:57.100
Second, she was
encouraging a coup.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.934
Third, why does
she get to text Mark Meadows?

00:06:59.934 --> 00:07:02.033
My wife doesn't get
to text my guests

00:07:02.033 --> 00:07:03.367
before they come on my show.

00:07:03.367 --> 00:07:07.200
Because if she did,
I knew what she would text them.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.868
[ Laughter ]

00:07:08.868 --> 00:07:10.901
This stuff is really deranged.

00:07:10.901 --> 00:07:13.901
She thought there were
secret watermarks on ballots

00:07:13.901 --> 00:07:17.734
and that the Biden crime family
was being detained at Gitmo

00:07:17.734 --> 00:07:18.934
for election fraud.

00:07:18.934 --> 00:07:20.567
On barges, no less.

00:07:20.567 --> 00:07:23.000
If you ask me, she's doing
disservice to the name Ginni.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:26.501
Ginni should be the cool aunt
who lets you have champagne

00:07:26.501 --> 00:07:28.334
at New Year's when you're 15,

00:07:28.334 --> 00:07:29.868
and drives a Jeep Wrangler

00:07:29.868 --> 00:07:31.334
with a bunch
of Phish stickers on it

00:07:31.334 --> 00:07:32.968
and has a cool roommate
named Debbie

00:07:32.968 --> 00:07:34.300
who has three
rescue dogs and --

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:35.634
Oh, I just think I...

00:07:35.634 --> 00:07:38.133
I think I just realized
something about Aunt Ginni.

00:07:38.133 --> 00:07:40.067
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.067 --> 00:07:42.868
Alright.

00:07:42.868 --> 00:07:44.367
Good for Aunt Ginni.

00:07:44.367 --> 00:07:45.601
Certainly...

00:07:45.601 --> 00:07:47.334
She's certainly doing better
than Aunt Barb.

00:07:47.334 --> 00:07:48.667
Aunt Barb!

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:51.767
Still looking for Mr. Right.

00:07:51.767 --> 00:07:54.434
In reality, of course,
it turned out the criminals

00:07:54.434 --> 00:07:55.968
were the ones
trying to overthrow

00:07:55.968 --> 00:07:58.000
a free and fair election
through violent means,

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.734
like the militia group
the Oath Keepers.

00:07:59.734 --> 00:08:03.434
Just today we found out that
the head of that group allegedly

00:08:03.434 --> 00:08:07.000
had a contact close to Trump
and tried to reach out to Trump

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.100
through an intermediary
during the coup.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.367
-New court papers have revealed

00:08:11.367 --> 00:08:14.534
just how far a north Texas man
was reportedly willing to go

00:08:14.534 --> 00:08:17.567
to overturn
the 2020 presidential election.

00:08:17.567 --> 00:08:20.834
Stuart Rhodes, the leader of the
Oath Keepers militia movement,

00:08:20.834 --> 00:08:22.601
allegedly called
an intermediary

00:08:22.601 --> 00:08:24.968
after the Capitol attack
on January 6th

00:08:24.968 --> 00:08:27.934
and asked to be put in contact
with former President Trump

00:08:27.934 --> 00:08:31.300
so that the president could
authorize their militia

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:34.067
to forcibly oppose
the transfer of power.

00:08:34.067 --> 00:08:36.634
-This individual denied Rhodes'
request to speak directly

00:08:36.634 --> 00:08:38.133
with President Trump.

00:08:38.133 --> 00:08:40.267
-He never got through to Trump,
but I'm guessing it's because

00:08:40.267 --> 00:08:42.667
Trump thought the Oath Keepers
was the name of a charity

00:08:42.667 --> 00:08:44.567
he promised to donate to
in the '80s.

00:08:44.567 --> 00:08:46.868
"Hi. We're calling
from the Oath Keepers Fund.

00:08:46.868 --> 00:08:50.367
We're trying to track down
a pledge for $1 million

00:08:50.367 --> 00:08:51.701
Mr. Trump made in 1984."

00:08:51.701 --> 00:08:52.934
[As Trump]
That's so weird.

00:08:52.934 --> 00:08:54.567
I could've sworn
I put the check in the mail.

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:55.767
Maybe it got lost --

00:08:55.767 --> 00:08:58.100
-♪ Blame it on the rain ♪

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:00.300
[ Laughter ]

00:09:04.968 --> 00:09:07.467
[Normal voice] You know, playing
a Milli Vanilli track early

00:09:07.467 --> 00:09:09.300
is how they caught
Milli Vanilli.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:11.300
[ Laughter ]

00:09:16.901 --> 00:09:19.567
You know what, I think
it's still gonna play.

00:09:19.567 --> 00:09:20.567
That's w--

00:09:20.567 --> 00:09:23.767
[ Laughing ]

00:09:23.767 --> 00:09:24.934
You guys, take it
out of your head.

00:09:24.934 --> 00:09:27.100
Get it out of your head.
Let it surprise you.

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:28.367
[As Trump] That's weird,
I could've sworn

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:29.501
I put the check
in the mail.

00:09:29.501 --> 00:09:30.968
Maybe it got lost
during a hurricane.

00:09:30.968 --> 00:09:32.100
I guess I'll have to...

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:34.400
-♪ Blame it on the rain ♪

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:38.734 --> 00:09:40.067
-'Cause the rain...

00:09:40.067 --> 00:09:41.934
Let me tell you something
about the rain.

00:09:41.934 --> 00:09:44.067
If I've learned...
The rain don't mind.

00:09:44.067 --> 00:09:45.801
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:48.968 --> 00:09:50.934
[ Laughter continues ]

00:09:50.934 --> 00:09:52.434
[Normal voice]
But let's get back to Roe.

00:09:52.434 --> 00:09:54.367
An extremist movement

00:09:54.367 --> 00:09:56.934
of far-right conservatives
who spent five decades

00:09:56.934 --> 00:09:59.701
carefully orchestrating
the outcome we're seeing now.

00:09:59.701 --> 00:10:02.200
Their devil's bargain with Trump
got them across the finish line,

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.701
but the assault
on abortion rights

00:10:03.701 --> 00:10:05.601
isn't unique to him,
and it didn't start with him.

00:10:05.601 --> 00:10:08.267
For example,
after the 1992 decision

00:10:08.267 --> 00:10:11.100
Planned Parenthood v. Casey
reaffirmed Roe,

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:13.400
anti-abortion activists
shifted to a new strategy.

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:16.400
They launched a barrage
of new abortion restrictions

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:19.033
to see which ones
the court would uphold.

00:10:19.033 --> 00:10:22.100
-The joint opinion delivered
by Justices O'Connor,

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.601
Souter, and Kennedy

00:10:23.601 --> 00:10:25.901
crafted a middle position.

00:10:25.901 --> 00:10:28.834
They upheld Roe,
but changed the standard

00:10:28.834 --> 00:10:31.200
by which abortion laws
would be judged.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:36.167
They established instead
the undue burden standard.

00:10:36.167 --> 00:10:38.601
A law would be invalid,
they declared,

00:10:38.601 --> 00:10:41.000
if it placed
substantial obstacles

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.868
in the path of a woman
seeking an abortion.

00:10:43.868 --> 00:10:46.267
-People got the impression
that abortion was safe,

00:10:46.267 --> 00:10:47.434
Roe v. Wade was safe.

00:10:47.434 --> 00:10:50.100
All the pro-choice people
went home.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:54.000
But what happened is pro-lifers
started to pass legislation

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:57.167
to test what exactly
is an undue burden.

00:10:57.167 --> 00:10:58.934
Let's pass this bill.
Is that undue?

